#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:2
msgid "Publishing a New Release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:5
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:7
msgid ""
"Check the current version on the latest ``main`` branch in ``mlx/version.h``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:8
msgid ""
"Push a new tag for current version to the GitHub repository, which would "
"automatically trigger release workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:10
msgid "Wait for the release workflow to **succeed**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:11
msgid ""
"Create a new GitHub Release for the latest tag from the `Tags <https://"
"github.com/ml-explore/mlx/tags>`__ page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:13
msgid "Create a pull request that increases the version in ``mlx/version.h``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:16
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:19
msgid "Build or test failure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:21
msgid "If the release workflow fails at the build or test step:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:23
msgid "Remove the tag from GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:24
msgid "Fix the build or test failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:25
msgid "Do the steps again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:27
msgid "See `Common causes of release build failures`_ for possible causes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:30
msgid "All publish jobs fail"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:32
msgid ""
"If all the publish jobs fail, remove the tag from GitHub first. A possible "
"cause is that the credentials are not valid anymore, you must get it fixed "
"before retrying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:37
msgid "Some publish jobs fail"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:39
msgid "If only some publish jobs fail, find the cause:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:41
msgid ""
"If the cause is a network issue, restart **only** the failed publish jobs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:42
msgid ""
"If restarting cannot fix the cause (for example, the package is larger than "
"the PyPI size limit), create a fix and merge it to the main branch. Then "
"`trigger the release workflow manually`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:47
msgid "Trigger the release workflow manually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:49
msgid ""
"Use this method only for troubleshooting. It is **not** the recommended way "
"to publish a release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:52
msgid "Open https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx/actions/workflows/release.yml."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:53
msgid ""
"For a dry run, which only tests that the release build works, keep the "
"\"Publish to PyPI\" option unchecked. Then click \"Run workflow\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:55
msgid ""
"To publish a release, select \"Publish to PyPI\". Then click \"Run "
"workflow\". Note that it is only possible to publish from main branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:59
msgid "Common causes of release build failures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:61
msgid ""
"Release build failures are rare, because pull requests run the full tests. "
"But the usual CI makes only debug builds, so a release build can fail "
"because:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:64
msgid ""
"Some code is inside a debug macro guard and behaves differently in release "
"builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:66
msgid ""
"A bug, for example a race condition, shows only when the code runs faster in "
"release builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:68
msgid ""
"In the CUDA build, the debug build targets only the current architecture, "
"while the release build targets all supported architectures, on which CUDA "
"code can fail to compile or run. So when changing a CUDA kernel that makes "
"use of hardware specific features, also start a dry run of the release build "
"to avoid such problems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/dev/release.rst:73
msgid ""
"The release build makes two Python packages: a frontend package with only "
"the Python bindings, and a backend package with the headers and the backend- "
"and platform-specific binaries. A change to the CMake files or ``setup.py`` "
"can break them. See ``.github/actions/build-wheel/action.yml`` for details."
msgstr ""
